{
  "abstract": "Measurements are reported of the differential cross section for the reaction \u03c0\u2212p\u2192\u03c0\u2212p,\u03c00n,and\u03b7n at three angles close to 180\u00b0 and for incident momenta in the range 0.6 to 1.0 GeV/c. The three measurements were made simultaneously at 1% intervals of beam momentum. The data on elastic scattering resolve a discrepancy between two earlier experiments. They also show clearly the effect of the opening of the \u03b7n channel. The charge-exchange data show that I-spin bounds are not violated in the kinematic region covered. The \u03b7n data can be adequately described with known s-channel resonances. No evidence for narrow N*'s is seen in any channel.",
